WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:58.615
May 1968 saw the beginning of the Paris Peace Talks.

00:00:59.136 --> 00:01:02.817
The intention was to stop the fighting between North and South Vietnam.

00:01:03.518 --> 00:01:07.923
Establish peace and remove the enormous American military presence.

00:01:08.504 --> 00:01:12.849
America had supported the South Vietnamese since 1955.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.292
Presidents John F.

00:01:14.331 --> 00:01:17.775
Kennedy and Lyndon Johnson had escalated America's involvement.

00:01:18.856 --> 00:01:22.459
resulting in more than 500,000 troops in Vietnam.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.602
In January 1969,

00:01:26.941 --> 00:01:32.725
Richard Nixon became president and faced extreme hostility to a war that had raged for so long.

00:01:33.346 --> 00:01:38.030
He assured the American public that he would withdraw the number of US troops considerably.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:39.210
However,

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.453
he initiated a secret plan and within two months was bombing Cambodia.

00:01:43.492 --> 00:01:43.992
you

00:01:47.468 --> 00:01:48.249
On September 2nd,

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.990
1969,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.990
President Ho Chi Minh,

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.272
hero of the revolution,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:54.112
dies.

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:57.695
He had been the father figure of the National Liberation Front,

00:01:58.115 --> 00:02:01.898
and had played an amazing game of bringing support from the Soviet Union,

00:02:02.198 --> 00:02:07.785
while
whilst keeping China at bay in his quest to rid Vietnam of the French and then the Americans.

00:02:07.805 --> 00:02:11.088
In 1969,

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:11.868
Ho Chi Minh died,

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.753
but the policy of Hanoi stayed the same.

00:02:15.754 --> 00:02:17.236
They were happy to sit around a table.

00:02:17.495 --> 00:02:17.995
in Paris,

00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:20.399
but would essentially agree nothing.

00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:26.122
Nixon had campaigned under his banner of peace with honour,

00:02:26.602 --> 00:02:33.108
which was the plan to build up the South Vietnamese forces so that they could defend the South against the communist North,

00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:34.669
or Vietnamisation.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.572
US troops would be gradually removed.

00:02:42.335 --> 00:02:46.579
The American life the last few years of the war was building up.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.441
Vietnamization,

00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:49.381
they called it.

00:02:49.382 --> 00:02:59.990
Vietnamization meant creating a South Vietnamese army which was going to salvage South Vietnam from the North Vietnamese evil communists.

00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:04.653
Nixon comes to office.

00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:05.395
He's pulling

00:03:05.775 --> 00:03:06.635
Americans out,

00:03:07.156 --> 00:03:10.639
and they're training up the South Vietnamese to fight their own battle.

00:03:11.098 --> 00:03:12.040
But a lot of these guys,

00:03:12.259 --> 00:03:16.683
they consider the Americans the really enemy as much as the communists fit.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.524
Vietnamese do,

00:03:18.104 --> 00:03:20.086
and they don't want to die fighting their brothers.

00:03:20.787 --> 00:03:22.609
So they're a pretty incompetent lot,

00:03:23.131 --> 00:03:24.171
the South Vietnamese army.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:32.539
I thought the South Vietnamese had behaved disgracefully during the war and then were treated disgracefully by the United States during the peace treaty.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.985
I think the South Vietnamese were exceptionally badly led from the time of Diem onwards.

00:03:40.044 --> 00:03:45.746
News broke out in November 1969 that there had been a massacre at the village of My Lai,

00:03:46.105 --> 00:03:50.768
where more than 400 villagers had been slaughtered by Lieutenant Calley and his troops.

00:03:53.508 --> 00:03:57.890
This village was not a stronghold of guerrillas.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.792
It was just an ordinary village.

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:04.477
There was a village nearby that was a stronghold of the Viet Cong,

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:05.878
but

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:07.000
Lieutenant Calley,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.462
who was in charge of the platoon,

00:04:08.622 --> 00:04:09.203
couldn't read a map.

00:04:09.603 --> 00:04:10.645
They went into this village,

00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:12.467
essentially shot everybody.

00:04:13.256 --> 00:04:15.277
...to the young women and then killed them.

00:04:15.718 --> 00:04:19.780
They threw one old man down a well and dropped a grenade in after him.

00:04:20.581 --> 00:04:21.261
Eventually,

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:29.086
the survivors were herded up into a drainage ditch and everyone just emptied their guns into the pile of bodies there.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.968
When you put young men in harm's way,

00:04:33.769 --> 00:04:34.569
they lose control.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.011
They shoot anything that moves,

00:04:37.012 --> 00:04:37.512
you know.

00:04:38.996 --> 00:04:40.917
And then you run into guys like Lieutenant Kelly,

00:04:41.378 --> 00:04:42.358
who were psychopaths.

00:04:43.619 --> 00:04:45.020
I'd venture to say there were

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.862
50 my lies that we never heard about.

00:04:50.143 --> 00:04:51.905
Kelly was sentenced to life.

00:04:52.565 --> 00:04:53.346
He served,

00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:53.866
I think,

00:04:53.946 --> 00:04:57.709
18 months under house arrest before being discharged.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.291
You know,
the Americans can't be doing this.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.742
Land of the free and trying to free the South.

00:05:05.902 --> 00:05:08.464
They can't be kidding the people they're coming here to defend.

00:05:09.444 --> 00:05:13.107
But I have to say that after a few years of being out there back and forth,

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.208
it was pretty commonplace.

00:05:15.408 --> 00:05:17.770
One of the most astonishing things that I can remember...

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.331
We met a colonel,

00:05:20.311 --> 00:05:22.132
a very well-educated American.

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:23.973
He spoke ancient Greek.

00:05:25.053 --> 00:05:27.054
He'd got a business degree from Harvard.

00:05:27.515 --> 00:05:28.155
Everywhere he went,

00:05:28.175 --> 00:05:29.255
he took his Thai chef.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.756
And he took French wine everywhere he went.

00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:32.977
It was just like a movie.

00:05:32.978 --> 00:05:35.198
I mean,
so much of Vietnam is like a movie.

00:05:39.596 --> 00:05:40.317
We interviewed him.

00:05:40.697 --> 00:05:41.098
Then he said,

00:05:41.098 --> 00:05:41.698
well,
gentlemen,

00:05:41.718 --> 00:05:42.378
thank you very much.

00:05:42.619 --> 00:05:44.400
I'm now off to kill Kong.

00:05:45.021 --> 00:05:46.362
I said,
you going on a mission,

00:05:46.402 --> 00:05:47.023
sir?
He said,

00:05:47.023 --> 00:05:47.703
no,
no.

00:05:47.723 --> 00:05:49.745
Every afternoon when there's nothing happening,

00:05:49.805 --> 00:05:50.426
I get in my

00:05:50.886 --> 00:05:56.211
Bell helicopter and I take my hunting rifle with me and I go and search for Kong.

00:05:56.591 --> 00:05:58.453
And if I see somebody in the fields,

00:05:58.513 --> 00:06:00.474
I give them a little bit of a run and then I kill them.

00:06:00.475 --> 00:06:01.816
There you go,

00:06:01.936 --> 00:06:03.237
Sarge.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:08.360
And I said,

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.400
you identify them?

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:09.721
He said,

00:06:09.721 --> 00:06:10.461
no,
no,

00:06:11.021 --> 00:06:11.881
I just kill them.

00:06:14.102 --> 00:06:16.703
So we said goodbye,

00:06:16.704 --> 00:06:18.043
and on the way back to Saigon,

00:06:18.223 --> 00:06:19.223
I said to the PIO,

00:06:19.323 --> 00:06:20.564
the press information man,

00:06:20.724 --> 00:06:21.724
a young kid,

00:06:21.784 --> 00:06:22.284
I said,

00:06:22.704 --> 00:06:23.925
he was pulling my plonker,

00:06:23.945 --> 00:06:24.465
wasn't he?

00:06:24.466 --> 00:06:24.966
I mean,

00:06:25.645 --> 00:06:26.705
he was pulling my leg.

00:06:28.146 --> 00:06:30.387
He goes out and shoots Kong in the afternoon?

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:31.127
Oh,
yes,

00:06:31.127 --> 00:06:31.648
sir,
he says,

00:06:31.648 --> 00:06:33.908
he just takes his hunting rifle and...

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.801
I said,
but the man's mad.

00:06:37.802 --> 00:06:38.142
He said,

00:06:38.142 --> 00:06:38.401
oh,
no,

00:06:38.401 --> 00:06:39.121
sir,
not mad.

00:06:39.822 --> 00:06:40.322
But,

00:06:40.423 --> 00:06:40.783
you know,

00:06:40.783 --> 00:06:41.623
when you live down there,

00:06:41.704 --> 00:06:44.005
you've got to do something like that in your spare time,

00:06:44.045 --> 00:06:45.866
otherwise a man could go crazy.

00:06:47.668 --> 00:06:53.612
Thousands of demonstrators opposed to the Vietnam War assembled in the nation's capital for a mass protest.

00:06:54.132 --> 00:06:57.955
The Paris peace talks are not moving forward with any sense of resolution.

00:06:58.455 --> 00:07:02.138
The American public are disgusted at the cover-up of the My Lai massacre.

00:07:03.279 --> 00:07:17.496
military police contain the crowd but clashes soon break out huge anti-war demonstrations converge on washington and outside american embassies in european cities the intense secret bombing of cambodia continues president

00:07:17.576 --> 00:07:20.820
Nixon will soon be under even more pressure to end the war.

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:27.268
A small group of Vietnamese seeking a confrontation marched at night on the South Vietnamese embassy.

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:30.713
Washington police used tear gas to drive them away.

00:07:31.193 --> 00:07:32.014
Arrests were made.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:34.473
President,

00:07:34.474 --> 00:07:38.435
some Americans believe this country is heading for revolution,

00:07:39.376 --> 00:07:47.561
and others believe that crime and dissent and violent demonstrations are leading us to an era of repression.

00:07:48.682 --> 00:07:50.284
This country is not headed for revolution.

00:07:51.385 --> 00:07:55.991
The very fact that we do have the safety valves of the right to dissent,

00:07:56.411 --> 00:08:03.640
the very fact that the President of the United States asked the district commissioners to waive their rule for 30 days notice for a down payment.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:04.220
demonstration.

00:08:05.061 --> 00:08:09.345
That fact is an indication that when you have that kind of safety valve,

00:08:09.365 --> 00:08:10.606
you're not going to have revolution,

00:08:10.666 --> 00:08:11.727
which comes from repression.

00:08:16.791 --> 00:08:19.032
As the hostilities in America continue,

00:08:19.413 --> 00:08:22.375
soldiers in Vietnam now have draftees amongst them,

00:08:22.815 --> 00:08:25.077
many of whom are voicing their distrust of the war,

00:08:25.458 --> 00:08:27.159
causing unrest in the ranks.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.221
For my entire tour of duty,

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:33.144
and I think by and large all of my soldier colleagues felt,

00:08:33.224 --> 00:08:33.724
you

00:08:34.165 --> 00:08:35.566
we were wasting our time.

00:08:37.187 --> 00:08:39.529
But we were being told to do it,

00:08:39.689 --> 00:08:40.530
and we were soldiers,

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:41.490
and we were good soldiers,

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.071
and so we did it.

00:08:42.431 --> 00:08:43.652
It's a very,

00:08:43.752 --> 00:08:44.093
very,

00:08:44.093 --> 00:08:45.634
very desperate terrain there.

00:08:46.494 --> 00:08:47.776
Once you started to move north,

00:08:47.816 --> 00:08:48.576
it became different.

00:08:48.577 --> 00:08:49.577
Of course,
you had mountains,

00:08:49.597 --> 00:08:50.097
you had

00:08:50.798 --> 00:08:52.559
Pleiku, Central Highlands,

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.401
but certainly in the south,

00:08:54.781 --> 00:08:59.385
you had vast areas of paddy fields that you had to go through.

00:09:00.366 --> 00:09:02.027
That's when you know a war is lost,

00:09:02.607 --> 00:09:03.268
and you're still there.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:05.589
there,
you're sort of the left behinds.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:14.174
You have no enthusiasm or any verve because you know that the cause might have seemed appealing five years ago,

00:09:14.434 --> 00:09:15.595
but it's gone,

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:17.596
so what are you doing in the jungle?

00:09:18.136 --> 00:09:22.459
Which is why so many Americans got hooked on drugs.

00:09:24.756 --> 00:09:26.077
There was no mental way out.

00:09:27.038 --> 00:09:28.999
It just didn't make any sense.

00:09:36.844 --> 00:09:39.466
The secrets of atrocities in Vietnam and

00:09:39.466 --> 00:09:42.009
and bombing in Cambodia break in the press.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.814
The US public are shocked and outrage takes hold.

00:09:45.815 --> 00:09:46.675
It's the time of the season for love.

00:09:59.881 --> 00:10:02.084
When Senate transcripts were made public,

00:10:02.485 --> 00:10:03.927
news of increased U.S.

00:10:03.987 --> 00:10:06.550
involvement in Cambodia and Laos surfaced.

00:10:07.051 --> 00:10:09.655
This leads to more demonstrations across America.

00:10:11.345 --> 00:10:15.706
When Richard Nixon announced that his troops were being committed to Cambodia,

00:10:15.947 --> 00:10:19.868
the anti-war movement was revived in America.

00:10:20.108 --> 00:10:29.911
Huge moratorium marches protesting against the war in Cambodia spread to all parts of America and to other places such as Australia.

00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:31.132
In some cases,

00:10:31.552 --> 00:10:32.052
the

00:10:32.172 --> 00:10:34.413
National Guard fired on protesters.

00:10:37.357 --> 00:10:39.559
Tragedy strikes at Kent University,

00:10:39.699 --> 00:10:41.580
Ohio in May 1970.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.362
Several anti-war protesters hurl rocks at the National Guard,

00:10:45.682 --> 00:10:47.303
who open fire on the crowd,

00:10:47.444 --> 00:10:48.844
killing four students.

00:10:50.806 --> 00:10:54.788
Gotta get down to it.

00:10:54.789 --> 00:10:55.489
Soldiers are cutting us down.

00:10:57.833 --> 00:11:00.715
Parents of America are shocked.

00:11:01.216 --> 00:11:04.899
These are nice middle-class kids who were shot down by their own people.

00:11:05.499 --> 00:11:09.342
Congress gets up in arms and essentially stops funding the war.

00:11:09.563 --> 00:11:13.406
They've stopped increasing the return of US troops from Vietnam.

00:11:19.931 --> 00:11:23.214
The Vietnam War suffers decreasing support in the US.

00:11:23.674 --> 00:11:26.937
President Nixon is forced into eliminating the use of the draft.

00:11:27.441 --> 00:11:29.843
With ongoing peace talks in Paris stalling,

00:11:30.123 --> 00:11:32.024
he introduces another peace plan.

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:34.947
With a continuing legacy of de-escalation,

00:11:35.267 --> 00:11:38.709
there were fears this was leading to a wider conflict in Indochina.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.391
The new president of North Vietnam,

00:11:41.591 --> 00:11:42.252
Le Duc Tho,

00:11:42.732 --> 00:11:47.476
and Henry Kissinger begin secret talks in an attempt to resolve the situation.

00:11:47.896 --> 00:11:51.038
The peace talks were not very successful,

00:11:51.439 --> 00:11:52.700
especially under Nixon.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:53.461
However,

00:11:53.461 --> 00:11:54.381
it was clear that

00:11:54.865 --> 00:11:57.666
The war could not be ended finally without an agreement.

00:11:57.986 --> 00:12:00.187
And during 1971,

00:12:00.188 --> 00:12:00.787
the U.S.

00:12:01.328 --> 00:12:07.670
conceded it would not oppose a continuation of the North Vietnamese troop presence in the South.

00:12:07.671 --> 00:12:11.352
In 1971,

00:12:11.353 --> 00:12:14.393
the New York Times publishes the Pentagon Papers.

00:12:15.173 --> 00:12:18.775
This shows an incredible legacy of deception concerning U.S.

00:12:18.855 --> 00:12:20.135
policy in Vietnam.

00:12:21.196 --> 00:12:23.717
President Nixon appeals to the Supreme Court.

00:12:24.101 --> 00:12:27.223
In an attempt to stop the publication of sensitive material.

00:12:27.823 --> 00:12:28.323
However,

00:12:28.323 --> 00:12:33.366
the court rules in favor of the New York Times and allows continued publication.

00:12:34.507 --> 00:12:36.268
Under pressure from the Democrats,

00:12:36.628 --> 00:12:43.311
Nixon changes his policy and orders the gradual reduction of 540,000 troops in Vietnam.

00:12:44.032 --> 00:12:46.753
What you had was the South Vietnamese army essentially fighting,

00:12:47.314 --> 00:12:51.576
backed by American air power and with some American advisers still there.

00:12:53.537 --> 00:12:56.319
The next step was the 1972

00:12:56.759 --> 00:12:58.180
North Vietnamese offensive,

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:03.764
which led to a revival in some parts of South Vietnam of the NLF guerrilla war.

00:13:05.745 --> 00:13:10.308
Vietnamese communists mobilised and used tanks in a conventional war style,

00:13:10.309 --> 00:13:11.509
which they hadn't used before.

00:13:11.589 --> 00:13:15.552
They drove across a demilitarised zone into South Vietnam,

00:13:15.612 --> 00:13:16.393
from North Vietnam.

00:13:16.953 --> 00:13:21.216
They captured various towns in the Saigon region,

00:13:21.236 --> 00:13:22.657
in particular a place called An Loc.

00:13:23.841 --> 00:13:32.083
And the United States bombing of North Vietnam indeed escalated through the year 1972 while the peace talks were going ahead.

00:13:32.884 --> 00:13:43.006
We have adopted a plan which we have worked out in cooperation with the South Vietnamese for the complete withdrawal of all US combat ground forces.

00:13:44.767 --> 00:13:52.949
President Nixon addresses the American public about withdrawing all US troops and therefore all involvement with the war in Vietnam.

00:13:53.857 --> 00:13:56.120
Ongoing secret peace talks are revealed.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:57.081
However,

00:13:57.081 --> 00:14:01.205
Nixon cannot stop himself from making more onslaughts in Cambodia.

00:14:09.906 --> 00:14:15.709
I think that the left-run people have gotten a lot better on the 527.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.471
No,
I read it.

00:14:16.471 --> 00:14:17.391
The nuclear bomb.

00:14:17.392 --> 00:14:17.892
That's actually...

00:14:17.911 --> 00:14:18.411
That,

00:14:19.112 --> 00:14:20.072
I think,

00:14:20.073 --> 00:14:21.834
would just be too much.

00:14:22.014 --> 00:14:23.495
The nuclear bomb.

00:14:23.496 --> 00:14:23.996
That probably...

00:14:26.556 --> 00:14:30.216
I just want you to think big,

00:14:30.217 --> 00:14:34.617
Henry,
for Christ's sake.

00:14:34.618 --> 00:14:39.538
He also wants to force the hand of the North Vietnamese to make concessions in these talks,

00:14:39.998 --> 00:14:43.959
so he orders the bombing of fuel storage areas near Hanoi and Haiphong.

00:14:44.379 --> 00:14:52.001
The administration makes it clear to the North Vietnamese that no area of Vietnam is off-limits to bombing raids.

00:14:53.925 --> 00:14:59.729
Nixon every so often stopped the bombing of the North to try and encourage them to say something.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:00.670
And when they didn't,

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.711
he started bombing them even more.

00:15:02.731 --> 00:15:04.753
And he attacked Hanoi and Haiphong,

00:15:04.953 --> 00:15:09.817
and they even mined the harbor at Haiphong to prevent suppliers getting in.

00:15:11.358 --> 00:15:12.539
The famous incident of

00:15:12.979 --> 00:15:13.479
Kim Phuc,

00:15:13.519 --> 00:15:16.641
the girl whose picture of her back burning with napalm,

00:15:16.802 --> 00:15:17.982
running down the street,

00:15:18.063 --> 00:15:19.764
that was about

00:15:20.144 --> 00:15:21.385
45 minutes out of Saigon.

00:15:21.805 --> 00:15:22.506
You felt the war.

00:15:23.126 --> 00:15:23.947
You could hear the bombing.

00:15:24.247 --> 00:15:26.429
There were rockets coming into Saigon from time to time.

00:15:26.729 --> 00:15:29.831
You'd wake up in the middle of the night and there'd be a shuddering blast.

00:15:32.353 --> 00:15:33.754
Napalming a village.

00:15:33.834 --> 00:15:34.334
I mean,

00:15:34.474 --> 00:15:38.317
to see a village suddenly destroyed in front of you by a simple napalm bomb,

00:15:38.918 --> 00:15:40.879
it was a pretty devastating thing to watch.

00:15:41.359 --> 00:15:42.820
Well,
a few weeks after I got into the country,

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.561
into my unit...

00:15:44.201 --> 00:15:45.602
Up on the side of a mountain,

00:15:45.962 --> 00:15:46.783
we got bushwhacked,

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:48.745
and the ambush came from above.

00:15:49.646 --> 00:15:51.207
And by the time everything was sorted out,

00:15:51.427 --> 00:15:52.248
a super saver,

00:15:52.348 --> 00:15:52.848
the F-100,

00:15:53.689 --> 00:15:58.253
came clambering up the valley and dropped its payload up above us.

00:15:59.133 --> 00:15:59.754
And it was napalm.

00:16:00.254 --> 00:16:02.016
And it was,

00:16:02.736 --> 00:16:04.278
you know,
red fire and black smoke,

00:16:04.598 --> 00:16:06.800
just like in the various war films you see.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.082
And it was far away not to get singed by it,

00:16:10.183 --> 00:16:12.965
but you could certainly feel the atmosphere change.

00:16:18.489 --> 00:16:26.035
Henry Kissinger and Le Duc Tho reach an agreement in principle on various key measures leading to a ceasefire in Vietnam.

00:16:26.455 --> 00:16:33.001
However the South Vietnamese President Chiu refuses to agree saying the war in the South is still ongoing.

00:16:34.842 --> 00:16:42.568
President Nixon has a bit of a problem because he's coming up to face a new election and he had promised peace and order and hadn't delivered it.

00:16:43.977 --> 00:16:52.623
So there's great pressure on him and his national security advisors at Henry Kissinger to get some peace agreement.

00:16:53.464 --> 00:16:54.284
At this point,

00:16:54.744 --> 00:16:56.626
the communist government in Hanoi,

00:16:57.566 --> 00:17:01.429
probably seeing the possibility of an agreement before the election,

00:17:02.049 --> 00:17:05.392
dropped its demand that the Thieu government be replaced.

00:17:06.032 --> 00:17:08.534
And this meant that an agreement was possible,

00:17:08.554 --> 00:17:10.835
and this was announced in October of

00:17:11.776 --> 00:17:13.297
1972. You just gotta...

00:17:15.318 --> 00:17:21.239
Its people have suffered much and they will remain there after we leave.

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:26.041
We believe that peace is at hand.

00:17:30.102 --> 00:17:35.963
The Americans just wanted to be out of the war and they were finding any way of doing it in peace with honor as they called it.

00:17:36.604 --> 00:17:41.045
They want to get the American army out of South Vietnam.

00:17:41.897 --> 00:17:45.840
And then the South Vietnamese government would fall and the communists would take over.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.521
They knew it was going to happen,

00:17:47.522 --> 00:17:51.524
it was just they didn't want it to happen the day after they left.

00:17:52.185 --> 00:17:56.608
The deal that President Chu wanted when it was clear that the Americans were going to cut a deal with the

00:17:57.388 --> 00:17:58.209
North Vietnamese,

00:17:58.249 --> 00:18:00.290
which would bring the American prisoners back home as well,

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:01.912
which was a huge issue in America,

00:18:02.452 --> 00:18:09.157
was that President Chu see that it was a very bad deal for South Vietnam because he wanted a deal whereby...

00:18:09.573 --> 00:18:11.173
The North Vietnamese troops would withdraw,

00:18:11.334 --> 00:18:15.035
and that was a deal that the Americans couldn't make the North Vietnamese agree to.

00:18:15.175 --> 00:18:18.296
So they put pressure on President Chiu to sign up to this peace agreement,

00:18:18.556 --> 00:18:19.696
which he did very reluctantly.

00:18:20.376 --> 00:18:29.099
We have ended the longest and most difficult war in our history in a way that maintained the trust of our allies and the respect of our adversaries.

00:18:30.959 --> 00:18:36.861
President Chiu is finally forced into signing with promises of aid against any further aggression from the North.

00:18:37.529 --> 00:18:39.531
The ceasefire is signed on January 28th,

00:18:39.532 --> 00:18:42.433
1973.

00:18:42.434 --> 00:18:44.134
Then the US troops withdrew.

00:18:44.234 --> 00:18:50.999
The North Vietnamese handed over the 500 or more prisoners of war who had been held in the north.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.661
Mostly pilots shot down there,

00:18:53.901 --> 00:18:57.524
and the agreement went ahead between Hanoi and the United States.

00:18:58.024 --> 00:18:58.605
For the Americans,

00:18:58.606 --> 00:18:59.485
the war was over.

00:18:59.646 --> 00:19:00.786
They got their prisoners home.

00:19:00.926 --> 00:19:01.607
They had lost

00:19:02.007 --> 00:19:03.008
55,000

00:19:03.488 --> 00:19:04.109
Americans.

00:19:04.389 --> 00:19:05.729
Out of that 55,000,

00:19:05.889 --> 00:19:07.910
half of them were 17 or 18-year-olds.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:09.951
It had been a traumatic experience for America,

00:19:10.471 --> 00:19:11.611
so they just wanted to get out.

00:19:13.272 --> 00:19:15.712
When the war ended in 1973,

00:19:16.212 --> 00:19:18.753
591 prisoners were returned.

00:19:19.253 --> 00:19:20.834
This was only about 12%

00:19:20.974 --> 00:19:22.674
of those requested by the US.

00:19:23.354 --> 00:19:27.376
What happened to the other 3,109 that were asked for?

00:19:27.976 --> 00:19:32.277
Henry Kissinger sent a secret letter to the North Vietnamese Prime Minister.

00:19:32.665 --> 00:19:39.089
that the US was willing to pay $3.2 billion for the return of the remaining prisoners of war.

00:19:39.629 --> 00:19:41.790
The US Senate voted against it.

00:19:42.751 --> 00:19:43.251
America,

00:19:43.611 --> 00:19:44.111
I felt,

00:19:44.352 --> 00:19:45.172
just wanted to forget,

00:19:45.192 --> 00:19:45.572
in a way,

00:19:45.572 --> 00:19:46.533
that Vietnam existed.

00:19:47.153 --> 00:19:48.654
After the signing of the Paris Peace Agreement,

00:19:48.814 --> 00:19:52.556
fighting continued for the South Vietnamese in South Vietnam,

00:19:52.857 --> 00:19:55.338
and 1,000 Vietnamese were dying a week.

00:19:55.598 --> 00:20:00.321
So in a year's casualties were more than the Americans suffered in the entire war.

00:20:08.524 --> 00:20:12.226
The last American combat soldiers leave South Vietnam.

00:20:12.746 --> 00:20:15.707
Though the military advisers and Marines protecting U.S.

00:20:15.767 --> 00:20:16.948
installations remain,

00:20:17.568 --> 00:20:18.128
the U.S.

00:20:18.208 --> 00:20:19.949
draft program is closed.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:26.112
The Nobel Peace Prize is given to Kissinger and Le Duc Tho.

00:20:26.792 --> 00:20:27.152
However,

00:20:27.152 --> 00:20:29.593
the North Vietnamese president does not accept it.

00:20:29.953 --> 00:20:31.994
As peace has not arrived in Vietnam,

00:20:32.514 --> 00:20:34.436
the North is still attacking the South.

00:20:36.757 --> 00:20:37.437
In America,

00:20:37.697 --> 00:20:40.219
President Nixon faces his own crisis.

00:20:40.759 --> 00:20:42.500
In June 1972,

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:52.606
a story in the Washington Post had reported that burglars had been arrested inside the office of the Democratic National Committee in the Watergate complex in Washington.

00:20:53.046 --> 00:20:58.229
The reporters Woodward and Bernstein would investigate the story until they found evidence

00:20:58.469 --> 00:21:04.792
that a $25,000 check from Nixon's reelection campaign had been given to one of the burglars.

00:21:05.733 --> 00:21:14.718
I believe that most anyone who worked at the White House during the past four years can attest to the concern that prevailed regarding any and all leagues.

00:21:15.438 --> 00:21:19.641
The full story of Nixon's aides became a huge political scandal.

00:21:20.221 --> 00:21:24.863
They had been running an election campaign employing spying and sabotage.

00:21:25.244 --> 00:21:27.645
I think it is time in this country to quit.

00:21:27.925 --> 00:21:34.113
making national heroes out of those who steal secrets and publish them in the newspapers.

00:21:36.376 --> 00:21:36.877
However,

00:21:37.177 --> 00:21:38.919
more secrets are revealed,

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:42.244
which will make Nixon's presidency untenable.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.080
In 1974,

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:55.662
President Chu announces resumption of war against the North Vietnamese,

00:21:55.982 --> 00:21:59.764
who have been encroaching on the South in violation of the peace treaty.

00:22:00.404 --> 00:22:05.967
Weakened by wave after wave of air attacks from America since 1969,

00:22:05.968 --> 00:22:09.448
neighboring Cambodia is vulnerable to its own rising threat,

00:22:09.928 --> 00:22:11.149
the Khmer Rouge.

00:22:15.923 --> 00:22:17.744
Cambodia is a case completely apart.

00:22:17.764 --> 00:22:18.144
I mean,

00:22:18.144 --> 00:22:31.812
it's never been equal in modern times because it was an attempt by a small coterie of Cambodian communist leaders to turn it into a utopian agrarian society and destroying all of its connections with the outside world.

00:22:32.372 --> 00:22:33.673
Once the Americans pulled out,

00:22:34.233 --> 00:22:38.535
the communists took over in Laos and then the Khmer Rouge,

00:22:38.875 --> 00:22:42.357
who were only a handful of communist guerrillas in there,

00:22:42.718 --> 00:22:45.259
managed to force out the compromised and weakened.

00:22:45.671 --> 00:22:48.734
Cambodian government ending in what,

00:22:48.894 --> 00:22:49.494
two million dead?

00:22:51.296 --> 00:22:59.042
The fallout from the Watergate scandal ultimately forces Nixon to resign from the presidency before being impeached.

00:22:59.822 --> 00:23:00.443
In leaving it,

00:23:00.603 --> 00:23:01.824
I do so with this prayer.

00:23:05.247 --> 00:23:10.992
May God's grace be with you in all the days ahead.

00:23:16.603 --> 00:23:18.184
In August 1974,

00:23:18.645 --> 00:23:19.886
Gerald Ford Jr.

00:23:20.066 --> 00:23:20.606
becomes the

00:23:21.267 --> 00:23:21.967
38th president.

00:23:23.128 --> 00:23:25.390
With American troops out of Vietnam,

00:23:25.751 --> 00:23:28.333
the press report events there less and less.

00:23:28.893 --> 00:23:31.115
The public has lost interest in the war.

00:23:32.536 --> 00:23:34.118
The Vietnam War,

00:23:34.638 --> 00:23:36.239
and it didn't concern Americans,

00:23:36.319 --> 00:23:39.782
particularly after all the coverage it had gotten for 10 years.

00:23:40.783 --> 00:23:41.944
It wasn't that big a story.

00:23:42.945 --> 00:23:45.267
I was on the telex with a foreign editor in New York.

00:23:46.747 --> 00:23:47.307
And I said,

00:23:47.987 --> 00:23:50.528
I'm catching a flight into Saigon tomorrow.

00:23:52.048 --> 00:23:52.769
And he said,

00:23:53.989 --> 00:23:56.550
are you volunteering to go to Vietnam?

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:01.251
I didn't quite understand what was going on.

00:24:02.611 --> 00:24:03.111
I said,

00:24:03.252 --> 00:24:04.312
I'm booked,

00:24:04.332 --> 00:24:05.272
I'm going in tomorrow.

00:24:05.292 --> 00:24:06.072
He said,

00:24:06.092 --> 00:24:07.173
you're volunteering to go.

00:24:08.813 --> 00:24:10.614
And I finally caught on.

00:24:11.354 --> 00:24:15.495
What he was doing was establishing on paper.

00:24:16.691 --> 00:24:19.714
That I was volunteering to go to Vietnam,

00:24:19.754 --> 00:24:23.497
that I was not being assigned to go to Vietnam.

00:24:24.278 --> 00:24:25.679
So that whatever happened,

00:24:26.440 --> 00:24:26.800
Hey,

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:27.461
he volunteered,

00:24:27.462 --> 00:24:28.122
we didn't make him go.

00:24:28.502 --> 00:24:29.603
We didn't even ask him to go.

00:24:30.083 --> 00:24:33.306
We didn't even suggest that he should go.

00:24:35.769 --> 00:24:37.310
You know how dangerous it is?

00:24:37.410 --> 00:24:40.273
Do you really want to go?

00:24:41.674 --> 00:24:42.495
Are you volunteering?

00:24:43.631 --> 00:24:44.692
So it just went on like that.

00:24:44.712 --> 00:24:45.212
So I kept,

00:24:45.373 --> 00:24:46.093
and eventually I said,

00:24:46.153 --> 00:24:46.493
yeah,

00:24:46.493 --> 00:24:47.194
I'm volunteering.

00:24:47.214 --> 00:24:47.834
I'm going to go.

00:24:49.195 --> 00:24:50.096
In Vietnam,

00:24:50.296 --> 00:24:54.760
President Chiu makes a mistake and withdraws all his troops from the north,

00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:56.301
causing mass panic.

00:24:56.901 --> 00:25:02.425
It's not long before the Viet Cong communists lay siege to the province just north of Saigon.

00:25:03.166 --> 00:25:05.808
There is no response from America.

00:25:06.648 --> 00:25:09.891
The Viet Cong move in on Hue and take the city.

00:25:11.751 --> 00:25:15.853
Just a few minutes ago we had confirmation that the city of Hue had fallen to the communists.

00:25:15.854 --> 00:25:21.797
It looks very much as if the North Vietnamese up there allowed these troops and these people to leave the beaches without firing on them,

00:25:21.857 --> 00:25:24.018
giving them a chance to get away before entering the city.

00:25:26.399 --> 00:25:26.860
The

00:25:26.860 --> 00:25:32.223
North Vietnamese gradually built up strength and decided that they would go for broke,

00:25:32.263 --> 00:25:33.844
that the Americans were not going to intervene.

00:25:33.964 --> 00:25:37.906
So they launched a lightning offensive and swept up the country,

00:25:38.046 --> 00:25:39.627
taking over provincial towns.

00:25:40.195 --> 00:25:40.996
North of Saigon.

00:25:41.776 --> 00:25:42.597
Early Monday morning,

00:25:42.617 --> 00:25:43.998
a Viet Cong Sapper unit,

00:25:44.899 --> 00:25:47.061
probably no more than 20 or 30 men and women,

00:25:47.541 --> 00:25:50.223
attacked and set fire to an American USAID installation,

00:25:50.744 --> 00:25:52.686
closing the bridge and Highway 1.

00:25:54.587 --> 00:25:59.131
The South Vietnamese Army simply cannot hold the line against the North Vietnamese,

00:25:59.132 --> 00:26:00.832
who are professional and dedicated,

00:26:01.032 --> 00:26:02.013
well-trained soldiers.

00:26:02.454 --> 00:26:08.599
Congress is now trying to wash its hands of the whole thing and is cutting back the budget for aid to the South Vietnamese.

00:26:08.967 --> 00:26:10.347
Being restricted with their armaments,

00:26:10.667 --> 00:26:11.568
they're getting nothing at all.

00:26:12.008 --> 00:26:21.931
President Chu made a huge strategic blunder in withdrawing the remnants of the South Vietnamese army from these threatened northern areas and to bring them around to Saigon to protect Saigon,

00:26:22.351 --> 00:26:26.012
which the result was that the rest of the country fell completely into the communist hands.

00:26:26.952 --> 00:26:28.292
And then it was just a matter of time,

00:26:28.332 --> 00:26:28.832
really.

00:26:30.033 --> 00:26:32.314
President Chu resigns reluctantly,

00:26:32.714 --> 00:26:33.834
stating that in the end,

00:26:33.994 --> 00:26:37.115
the South Vietnamese had been let down by the Americans.

00:26:37.715 --> 00:26:42.539
The North Vietnamese army seized the opportunity and closed in on Saigon.

00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:47.403
America needed to get as many of its remaining people out from the embassy,

00:26:47.783 --> 00:26:49.865
sending in all available helicopters.

00:26:50.425 --> 00:26:55.349
The Vietnamese also sensed the communist advance was close and were desperate to flee.

00:26:55.970 --> 00:26:57.671
Panic engulfed Saigon.

00:27:00.093 --> 00:27:02.796
I'll tell you one thing which was really interesting,

00:27:02.836 --> 00:27:04.537
which I don't think it's been reported that much.

00:27:05.378 --> 00:27:06.779
In the big

00:27:07.595 --> 00:27:12.376
In the parking lot of the embassy there was a beautiful tree and the ambassador,

00:27:12.436 --> 00:27:13.156
Graham Martin,

00:27:13.377 --> 00:27:14.537
refused to cut down the tree.

00:27:15.617 --> 00:27:17.678
The CIA was going to him and saying,

00:27:17.978 --> 00:27:24.500
cut down that tree because this is where the helicopters are going to land,

00:27:25.320 --> 00:27:26.300
will have to land,

00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:28.781
and Martin refused.

00:27:30.101 --> 00:27:36.963
The docks on Tuesday morning were crammed with thousands of Vietnamese desperate to escape from Saigon by any means possible.

00:27:37.811 --> 00:27:43.714
I remember filming in Saigon where mothers were throwing their babies to strangers on the ship.

00:27:44.354 --> 00:27:45.774
Literally throwing them like a bit of,

00:27:46.035 --> 00:27:46.735
like a parcel.

00:27:47.915 --> 00:27:48.836
Save my babies.

00:27:49.256 --> 00:27:50.417
Throwing their babies on board.

00:27:50.757 --> 00:27:56.199
You saw soldiers stripping off their uniforms and fighting almost naked to get on boats.

00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:01.641
Many people died because their flimsy craft had sunk.

00:28:01.861 --> 00:28:03.222
They were often overloaded.

00:28:03.223 --> 00:28:04.763
They were attacked by pirates.

00:28:05.836 --> 00:28:06.336
killed,

00:28:06.336 --> 00:28:08.678
it was a general disaster.

00:28:08.978 --> 00:28:14.481
The Americans actually sent some aircraft in to airlift their own Vietnamese employees out of their embassies.

00:28:15.101 --> 00:28:17.302
We had been told by the CIA,

00:28:17.943 --> 00:28:22.125
we expect to evacuate within the next 24 hours,

00:28:22.445 --> 00:28:23.285
36 hours.

00:28:23.966 --> 00:28:26.467
What we don't want is for you guys to panic.

00:28:27.027 --> 00:28:31.070
So we've arranged there will be a signal broadcast by AFN,

00:28:31.190 --> 00:28:32.450
American Forces Network,

00:28:32.630 --> 00:28:35.212
they said it'll be Bing Crosby singing White Christmas.

00:28:36.180 --> 00:28:38.301
Imagine it's 115 degrees outside.

00:28:38.681 --> 00:28:51.807
Could you think of anything so incredible that Bing Crosby singing I'm Dreaming of a White Christmas would be the signal that the evacuation had begun?

00:28:52.667 --> 00:28:54.368
And when they told us in advance,

00:28:54.369 --> 00:28:55.569
a couple of days in advance,

00:28:56.089 --> 00:28:57.109
that this would be it,

00:28:57.430 --> 00:28:58.430
we thought they were joking.

00:29:01.731 --> 00:29:02.392
By that time...

00:29:03.052 --> 00:29:08.074
Embassy is surrounded by thousands of Vietnamese all trying to get into the compound.

00:29:08.855 --> 00:29:13.456
And we really had to fight and claw our way through this crowd to get to the wall.

00:29:14.057 --> 00:29:14.497
People,

00:29:14.497 --> 00:29:19.039
lorries and cars all chasing one American evacuation convoy after the other.

00:29:20.159 --> 00:29:22.920
Jams that the Vietnamese police tried to clear with their rifles.

00:29:23.421 --> 00:29:24.981
But people were no longer afraid of them.

00:29:25.562 --> 00:29:27.663
There was now so much more to be afraid of.

00:29:29.283 --> 00:29:30.924
When we finally got to the wall.

00:29:32.056 --> 00:29:35.277
Marines had to really reach down and pull us up.

00:29:35.477 --> 00:29:36.018
And then,
you know,

00:29:36.018 --> 00:29:37.318
we see we're being pulled up,

00:29:37.358 --> 00:29:38.519
but all the people around us,

00:29:38.539 --> 00:29:40.660
including lovely kids,

00:29:41.580 --> 00:29:42.660
were not being pulled up.

00:29:43.381 --> 00:29:44.821
But then suddenly we too,

00:29:45.362 --> 00:29:48.043
the 40 or 50 of us in the safety of the coaches,

00:29:48.463 --> 00:29:55.846
had to get out and fight our way to the American compound where the helicopters were landing to fly us and the thousands more out of the country.

00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:59.187
And you had pictures,

00:29:59.508 --> 00:30:00.288
movie pictures.

00:30:01.312 --> 00:30:03.834
Of the Americans on the plane punching,

00:30:03.854 --> 00:30:05.315
actually punching people off.

00:30:05.955 --> 00:30:13.119
And you had helicopters flying off with people hanging on the skids and then dropping off.

00:30:13.719 --> 00:30:15.620
They were so desperate to escape.

00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:16.621
We did fight,

00:30:16.661 --> 00:30:17.381
we did claw.

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:19.822
I remember saying in my commentary that

00:30:20.623 --> 00:30:22.284
I wasn't proud of what I did that day.

00:30:23.004 --> 00:30:26.186
But we got to the wall and the Marines were pulling us up,

00:30:26.906 --> 00:30:29.728
punching the Vietnamese and pulling us up over the top.

00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:32.501
He hauled us up,

00:30:32.641 --> 00:30:36.104
kicking and punching Vietnamese who were clambering over our bodies.

00:30:38.245 --> 00:30:40.087
Ashamed and exhausted,

00:30:40.647 --> 00:30:47.333
we took our turn in the long crowd of refugees inside the embassy compound and waited for the helicopters to come down for us.

00:30:48.934 --> 00:30:50.515
I've been doing this for 48 years,

00:30:51.356 --> 00:30:53.798
and I think that's number one on my list.

00:30:54.559 --> 00:30:56.240
The last day of Saigon,

00:30:57.221 --> 00:30:59.423
the Americans losing their first war,

00:31:00.263 --> 00:31:00.763
leaving.

00:31:01.924 --> 00:31:12.091
From the American embassy to go to a ship in the South China Sea that was an admission of defeat.

00:31:13.712 --> 00:31:15.633
In the helicopter that took us out,

00:31:16.954 --> 00:31:19.736
it was open in the rear and I was just lying down on my stomach,

00:31:20.336 --> 00:31:24.059
looking out the back of the helicopter,

00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:26.621
saying goodbye to Saigon.

00:31:29.262 --> 00:31:29.762
And for me,

00:31:29.943 --> 00:31:31.464
I think for all of us who were there.

00:31:33.336 --> 00:31:35.902
And not meaning any disrespect,

00:31:36.363 --> 00:31:38.909
it'll never be Ho Chi Minh City in Saigon.

00:31:51.029 --> 00:31:55.331
Twenty years since America first began financing the South Vietnamese,

00:31:55.691 --> 00:31:57.692
it was finally out of Vietnam.

00:31:58.312 --> 00:32:00.993
In the desperation to get as many people to safety,

00:32:01.333 --> 00:32:05.735
the carriers at sea struggled to cope with the mass of fleeing people.

00:32:07.076 --> 00:32:09.016
The carriers were so full of helicopters,

00:32:09.017 --> 00:32:14.339
they were having to push helicopters that were very expensive over the side so others could land.

00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:18.660
In the general chaos of the situation,

00:32:19.060 --> 00:32:20.181
the Americans did not...

00:32:20.381 --> 00:32:21.481
burn the files,

00:32:21.661 --> 00:32:22.322
secret files,

00:32:22.422 --> 00:32:23.922
in their embassy.

00:32:24.682 --> 00:32:25.562
So when the

00:32:26.103 --> 00:32:27.943
North Vietnamese army turned up,

00:32:28.043 --> 00:32:32.784
the communists knew exactly who had been working for the Americans,

00:32:33.085 --> 00:32:34.165
and of course these people,

00:32:34.525 --> 00:32:35.325
if they weren't killed,

00:32:35.665 --> 00:32:37.226
were sent to re-education camps.

00:32:38.326 --> 00:32:40.927
A former general called Bich Minh became president,

00:32:41.087 --> 00:32:43.187
and the communists knew that there was nothing stopping them.

00:32:43.207 --> 00:32:44.908
They were militarily superior.

00:32:45.288 --> 00:32:48.889
The Americans weren't going to intervene to stop them taking Saigon.

00:32:49.465 --> 00:32:51.687
And they just rolled on relentlessly.

00:32:52.667 --> 00:32:56.010
When a tank turns up at the government house in Saigon,

00:32:56.390 --> 00:32:57.030
it's all over.

00:32:57.130 --> 00:32:59.532
The new interim president is told,

00:32:59.732 --> 00:33:02.134
you can't surrender what you don't have.

00:33:02.135 --> 00:33:02.975
He didn't have any power,

00:33:02.976 --> 00:33:03.855
he didn't have any troops,

00:33:03.895 --> 00:33:06.177
so it's just all over.

00:33:06.597 --> 00:33:08.178
The communist side wins.

00:33:08.238 --> 00:33:09.059
It's a victory for

00:33:10.340 --> 00:33:11.000
North Vietnam,

00:33:11.220 --> 00:33:12.281
the Democratic Republic,

00:33:12.441 --> 00:33:14.663
along with its fighters in the South.

00:33:15.844 --> 00:33:16.984
And for a year or so,

00:33:17.165 --> 00:33:17.665
you have...

00:33:18.065 --> 00:33:20.306
The two countries continue to exist side by side.

00:33:20.326 --> 00:33:21.507
In 1976,

00:33:21.587 --> 00:33:24.108
the countries emerged into form the Socialist Republic,

00:33:24.389 --> 00:33:24.969
one country,

00:33:25.749 --> 00:33:26.470
the culmination,

00:33:26.530 --> 00:33:30.592
really,
of what Ho Chi Minh and the other nationalists had been calling for,

00:33:30.672 --> 00:33:31.272
fighting for,

00:33:31.773 --> 00:33:33.254
ever since 1945.

00:33:33.474 --> 00:33:35.235
The new Socialist Republic of

00:33:35.655 --> 00:33:40.578
Vietnam is declared with its new capital in Hanoi,

00:33:41.058 --> 00:33:43.859
and Saigon is renamed Ho Chi Minh City.

00:33:44.560 --> 00:33:46.681
A very harsh period.

00:33:47.273 --> 00:33:48.874
...then happened in South Vietnam.

00:33:49.714 --> 00:33:56.238
Soldiers ended up in re-education camps all over the country and taken up to North Vietnam and put into camps.

00:33:56.698 --> 00:33:57.619
Many of them died.

00:33:57.859 --> 00:34:01.981
They tried to impose hardline socialist,

00:34:02.341 --> 00:34:04.763
Stalinist economic methods on the South.

00:34:05.223 --> 00:34:06.844
And the result is almost starvation.

00:34:08.625 --> 00:34:14.248
When the Camaros attacked our provinces in the West,

00:34:14.528 --> 00:34:16.209
my heart is with my country.

00:34:17.325 --> 00:34:17.825
And

00:34:18.145 --> 00:34:19.366
I wrote article.

00:34:21.466 --> 00:34:27.168
They found that in that article there was some kind of fire in there,

00:34:28.548 --> 00:34:32.669
some kind of love in there.

00:34:33.790 --> 00:34:34.710
And they took me,

00:34:35.070 --> 00:34:39.411
the communists took me aside.

00:34:41.772 --> 00:34:46.033
And they asked me to spy on my colleagues.

00:34:46.681 --> 00:34:48.723
And I cannot do without.

00:34:49.423 --> 00:34:49.923
And

00:34:50.104 --> 00:34:53.407
I started to think of running away.

00:34:56.890 --> 00:34:57.570
In America,

00:34:57.931 --> 00:35:02.795
Jimmy Carter is elected president and issues a pardon to all the draft Dodgers.

00:35:02.796 --> 00:35:06.958
In 1978,

00:35:07.198 --> 00:35:12.243
the Socialist Republic of Vietnam invades Cambodia and defeats the Khmer Rouge,

00:35:12.603 --> 00:35:14.965
forcing them back into their jungle refuges.

00:35:15.205 --> 00:35:16.326
on the Laos border.

00:35:23.871 --> 00:35:24.792
The outside world,

00:35:25.232 --> 00:35:27.374
whether it be the United States and Europe,

00:35:27.814 --> 00:35:31.557
is fearful of what Vietnam intends to do in Southeast Asia,

00:35:31.657 --> 00:35:36.360
and so they actually condemn and impose sanctions on the Vietnamese for getting rid of the Khmer Rouge.

00:35:37.381 --> 00:35:41.524
China decides to invade Vietnam and takes border cities,

00:35:42.024 --> 00:35:42.845
giving the warning...

00:35:43.065 --> 00:35:45.086
The gate to Hanoi is open.

00:35:46.186 --> 00:35:51.567
The Vietnamese put up a very stirring defence and gave the Chinese a bit of a bloody nose.

00:35:51.787 --> 00:35:55.108
And so Vietnam is almost completely isolated internationally.

00:35:55.109 --> 00:36:01.090
It's only friends with the Soviet Union and the Soviet bloc from 1979 right the way through the

00:36:01.710 --> 00:36:02.911
1980s. This is a very,

00:36:02.991 --> 00:36:04.371
very tough time in Vietnam.

00:36:05.451 --> 00:36:09.352
The ravages of war have destroyed the agricultural base of these societies.

00:36:10.092 --> 00:36:11.713
Entire villages have been decimated.

00:36:12.265 --> 00:36:14.166
People forced to abandon their lands.

00:36:14.946 --> 00:36:16.846
From being net exporters of rice,

00:36:17.327 --> 00:36:20.267
many regions of Southeast Asia have become net importers.

00:36:21.088 --> 00:36:23.188
The pride of self-sufficiency is gone.

00:36:23.889 --> 00:36:30.051
What is left for millions of people is dependency on aid from the outside and the long search for a new life.

00:36:32.171 --> 00:36:37.813
Many were desperate to escape the communist government and the terrible conditions they were forced to endure.

00:36:38.557 --> 00:36:42.731
Many Vietnamese try to flee en masse in heavily overcrowded boats.

00:36:43.814 --> 00:36:46.001
I pretend to be a child.

00:36:48.382 --> 00:36:53.603
I pay the gold to Chinese boat master.

00:36:55.284 --> 00:36:58.144
So we three,

00:36:59.225 --> 00:36:59.725
myself,

00:36:59.865 --> 00:37:00.885
my wife,

00:37:00.925 --> 00:37:01.645
and my baby,

00:37:02.306 --> 00:37:03.466
we went down to the

00:37:04.106 --> 00:37:05.506
Mekong River Delta.

00:37:06.347 --> 00:37:10.288
Our wooden boat is about 25 meters long.

00:37:11.068 --> 00:37:11.628
It got

00:37:12.368 --> 00:37:14.729
650 something.

00:37:15.517 --> 00:37:16.017
People.

00:37:16.478 --> 00:37:20.561
So even when it was still not moving yet,

00:37:21.382 --> 00:37:28.308
people in the boats started to suffer already because we did not have enough air to breathe.

00:37:28.309 --> 00:37:37.976
We were in the sea for just two days when the engine got into trouble.

00:37:38.036 --> 00:37:43.541
Every light gone out and in the dark you can hear everyone.

00:37:46.657 --> 00:37:54.900
I put my wife and my daughter in a very dangerous situation,

00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:55.760
but it was too late.

00:37:56.560 --> 00:37:57.060
And

00:37:57.220 --> 00:37:59.081
I accused myself.

00:37:59.581 --> 00:38:00.081
The

00:38:00.121 --> 00:38:03.562
British commercial ship passed by.

00:38:04.122 --> 00:38:11.745
The wife of the captain asked to return to pick us because she saw people from our ship.

00:38:12.285 --> 00:38:13.085
We were lucky.

00:38:14.137 --> 00:38:17.039
And then the ship took all of us to

00:38:17.379 --> 00:38:17.879
Hong Kong.

00:38:18.220 --> 00:38:20.482
All of us were put into the prison.

00:38:21.382 --> 00:38:23.444
We were there for four weeks.

00:38:24.165 --> 00:38:24.925
At the end,

00:38:25.145 --> 00:38:29.468
we signed a paper with the

00:38:30.449 --> 00:38:38.095
IOCM to borrow from them the money to get tickets,

00:38:38.275 --> 00:38:40.036
one-way tickets from Hong Kong to

00:38:40.537 --> 00:38:41.037
England.

00:38:42.345 --> 00:38:45.107
For those Vietnamese who didn't get out of Vietnam,

00:38:45.447 --> 00:38:47.989
the extremely difficult times continued.

00:38:48.569 --> 00:38:58.096
The report on the devastating effects of Agent Orange is revealed both in Vietnam and to the US veterans involved in the deployment of the toxic mix.

00:39:05.645 --> 00:39:16.234
The moon's sinking from the weight of the load In the building straight to sky Some of the most beautiful countryside in the world was just a desert.

00:39:17.175 --> 00:39:19.757
There were bomb craters where there should have been fields.

00:39:20.237 --> 00:39:23.780
Agent Orange was causing all sorts of birth defects in shore.

00:39:24.861 --> 00:39:33.308
I don't think that when the Americans were defoliating areas of Vietnam they were intending to leave a long-lasting injuries in terms of future generations were going to...

00:39:34.069 --> 00:39:36.770
be malformed as a result of these dioxins,

00:39:36.771 --> 00:39:38.791
these chemicals which have been dropped on them.

00:39:38.811 --> 00:39:40.092
That really wasn't the intention.

00:39:40.232 --> 00:39:42.533
But that in certain parts of Vietnam is what has happened.

00:39:46.295 --> 00:39:50.737
Paul Reuterschen had been in contact with Agent Orange in the Vietnam War.

00:39:51.097 --> 00:39:55.800
Shortly before his death from abdominal cancer in December 1978,

00:39:55.801 --> 00:39:58.521
he founded Agent Orange Victims International.

00:39:58.909 --> 00:40:01.451
which fought for compensation for US soldiers,

00:40:01.751 --> 00:40:07.255
filing multiple lawsuits against the six chemical companies in the US that produced Agent Orange,

00:40:07.695 --> 00:40:08.636
most significantly,

00:40:08.816 --> 00:40:10.357
Dow and Monsanto.

00:40:11.437 --> 00:40:16.281
The class action case was settled in 1984 for $180 million.

00:40:17.081 --> 00:40:19.383
Of the 105,000 claims,

00:40:19.683 --> 00:40:24.886
approximately 52,000 Vietnam veterans or their survivors received cash payments,

00:40:25.307 --> 00:40:28.189
which average only $3,800 each.

00:40:29.969 --> 00:40:31.050
In 1982,

00:40:31.330 --> 00:40:35.351
as a tribute to the thousands of US soldiers who died in Vietnam,

00:40:35.771 --> 00:40:38.112
a veterans memorial opened in Washington.

00:40:38.712 --> 00:40:39.212
However,

00:40:39.312 --> 00:40:43.933
the Vietnam veterans who survived have never been given the support they deserve.

00:40:44.633 --> 00:40:46.514
After the takeover of the communists,

00:40:46.854 --> 00:40:50.375
Vietnam was left with a legacy of extreme war damage,

00:40:50.755 --> 00:40:53.636
unexploded bombs and an impoverished economy.

00:40:54.316 --> 00:40:58.357
America dropped 7.8 million tons of bombs on Vietnam.

00:40:58.917 --> 00:41:02.138
more than it unleashed on Germany and Japan combined.

00:41:04.519 --> 00:41:08.020
We were back there for one of their independence days.

00:41:08.440 --> 00:41:15.042
They had this communist parade down the main street of Saigon up to the presidential palace.

00:41:15.602 --> 00:41:17.882
Jap and the others were there,

00:41:17.922 --> 00:41:19.103
the old soldiers,

00:41:19.104 --> 00:41:20.083
the old liberators.

00:41:21.063 --> 00:41:23.164
And when you were on a tight shot,

00:41:23.224 --> 00:41:23.864
you were on them.

00:41:24.464 --> 00:41:27.125
When you widened up behind them on the roofs of buildings...

00:41:27.613 --> 00:41:30.754
Or advertisements for Sony and Sanyo and Toyota.

00:41:31.635 --> 00:41:32.135
So,

00:41:32.655 --> 00:41:33.155
communism?

00:41:33.976 --> 00:41:34.696
Who won the war?

00:41:36.937 --> 00:41:39.058
There always were coffee plantations in South Vietnam,

00:41:39.059 --> 00:41:39.958
in the Central Highlands.

00:41:39.959 --> 00:41:40.619
The French had them,

00:41:40.979 --> 00:41:45.501
but the Vietnamese did clear out the land and build up these coffee plantations.

00:41:45.621 --> 00:41:46.021
Vietnam.

00:41:46.021 --> 00:41:48.522
has become the world's second largest coffee producer.

00:41:49.043 --> 00:41:50.203
It took most of the

00:41:51.364 --> 00:41:54.906
1980s for the Vietnamese to extricate themselves from Cambodia,

00:41:55.386 --> 00:41:58.988
renegotiating their relations with the outside world.

00:41:59.708 --> 00:42:03.711
By gradually allowing more and more freedom at the local economic level,

00:42:04.011 --> 00:42:11.735
the country was able to feed itself again and get to the position where Vietnam is the second largest rice exporter in the world.

00:42:14.356 --> 00:42:15.437
In recent years,

00:42:15.777 --> 00:42:19.618
Vietnam has become one of the fastest growing global economies.

00:42:19.958 --> 00:42:22.479
It is a significant agricultural exporter,

00:42:22.839 --> 00:42:25.280
the third largest oil producer in Asia,

00:42:25.740 --> 00:42:28.201
and an important manufacturer of textiles,

00:42:28.521 --> 00:42:29.061
clothing,

00:42:29.341 --> 00:42:31.702
and computer and mobile phone components.

00:42:32.742 --> 00:42:36.043
Estimates of its population exceed 92 million.

00:42:38.203 --> 00:42:38.703
Even now,

00:42:38.704 --> 00:42:41.024
Vietnam remains a communist country,

00:42:41.144 --> 00:42:43.245
despite all the trappings of...

00:42:43.585 --> 00:42:45.946
motorbikes and advertising and all that sort of thing that you see.

00:42:46.366 --> 00:42:55.628
The Communist Party is still in charge of the organisation of the economy and it still sees a big role for the state and it has big agricultural enterprises.

00:42:57.189 --> 00:42:59.309
Vietnam has become actually quite successful,

00:42:59.529 --> 00:43:02.450
but there is still a lot of press censorship,

00:43:02.810 --> 00:43:04.791
quite a lot of oppression if you get out of line.

00:43:05.231 --> 00:43:11.573
But it's also the economy of South Vietnam has been helped by a return of South Vietnamese boat people who've gone to America,

00:43:11.613 --> 00:43:12.153
for example.

00:43:12.613 --> 00:43:16.955
So many of the Vietnamese who've come to the States have done so well.

00:43:18.295 --> 00:43:19.235
And it was predictable.

00:43:19.255 --> 00:43:25.277
And these weren't the rich Vietnamese who managed to get out six months before the end of the war.

00:43:25.558 --> 00:43:33.820
These were boat people who are now doing so well in this country and have been doing so well in this country for a couple of decades now.

00:43:34.100 --> 00:43:35.461
And they've gone back home.

00:43:36.273 --> 00:43:38.455
...to South Vietnam and set up businesses there.

00:43:38.456 --> 00:43:41.156
So the country is quite dependent on an enormous amount of money...

00:43:41.196 --> 00:43:43.138
...that comes in from the Vietnamese diaspora.

00:43:43.158 --> 00:43:46.360
The Vietnam we knew during the war...

00:43:47.581 --> 00:43:52.825
...had a lot more reality to it.

00:43:54.646 --> 00:43:56.367
Saigon itself has changed enormously.

00:43:56.607 --> 00:43:59.489
A lot of the old French buildings have been torn down...

00:43:59.549 --> 00:44:01.851
...and buildings are high-rises with marble and glass...

00:44:02.391 --> 00:44:04.913
...and Louis Vuitton shops and Prada shops.

00:44:05.153 --> 00:44:05.853
I asked myself,

00:44:05.893 --> 00:44:06.253
I said,

00:44:06.253 --> 00:44:06.753
you know,

00:44:07.954 --> 00:44:11.895
is this really what these Vietnamese communists were fighting for?

00:44:11.896 --> 00:44:15.156
There's no question that as soon as the war was over,

00:44:15.916 --> 00:44:17.176
they began building an economy.

00:44:18.357 --> 00:44:20.057
And look at Vietnam today.

00:44:22.458 --> 00:44:25.218
Knowing that you lied,

00:44:25.659 --> 00:44:27.959
spade-faced while I cried,

00:44:29.760 --> 00:44:33.581
still I'd look to find the reason to believe.

00:44:38.583 --> 00:44:45.666
Thank you.

